            <ArticleTitle>Cancer-induced bone disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>48-56; quiz 57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A diagnosis of bone metastases may be devastating for patients with cancer because it suggests that the cancer is incurable and that patients are at increased risk of developing skeletal-related events. The optimal goal for these patients should be to maintain quality of life. Nurses have an important role in the care of patients with cancer-induced bone disease and need to have a good understanding of the effects of bone metastases to ensure prompt management of this condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
